  "body": "TO VIEW PROPERTY, PLEASE CLICK \"REQUEST A VIEWING\" BELOW, OR CALL OR TEXT. THANKS! :-)\r\n\r\nFor sale only for the second time in almost 50 years, this three bedroom, fully insulated pine weatherboard house is within walking distance to quiet Army Bay beach and beautiful Shakespear Regional Park.\r\n\r\nPerfect as a first home or holiday home, this would also suit a savvy investor or anyone looking to add further value. The property is private, fully fenced with a massive north-facing rear lawn that provides room to extend the house, add additional structures or a pool and create an outdoor entertaining paradise, subject to council consent. On a full site section of 809sqm, with a huge 11.2m x 4.6m garage and additional exterior parking for another 4-5 vehicles, there is ample room for your boat, kayaks, classic cars, home business or dream garage workshop. House + Garage = 160sqm area total.\r\n\r\nLovingly restored and upgraded, the current owners have enhanced this property significantly in their ownership, including; both house and garage exterior repainted/re-stained, house roof replaced with long-run Coloursteel, Expol underfloor insulation installed, upgraded remote garage door opener, house interior repainted, rear deck and front entranceway steps rebuilt, landscaped and planted out front of section to add additional 3 exterior car parks and garden boardwalk, replaced all carpet (downstairs carpet is brand new), upgraded front fence, brand new Panasonic heat pump, externally vented extractor fans in bathroom and range hood, converted garage guttering to Marley system, brand new shower wall lining and shower tap-ware and toilet, water tank drained/inspected/repaired/cleaned and repainted, replaced water pump, picket fence and gates installed to secure back yard for kids and pets.\r\n\r\nThe house still retains much of its original character, including the original early 1980's orange kitchen wall tiles and stainless bench top, rimu veneer doors, rear deck railings and exposed internal pine beams. While not essential, there is opportunity to add further value by modernising both kitchen and bathroom and potentially converting the kitchen and living to a more open plan layout, subject to builder survey.\r\n\r\nSet back from the road, the house is quiet, cosy and warm, thanks to Pink Batts in external walls and under roof and Expol underfloor insulation, with the rear verandah sheltering the house and sliding door from most inclement weather. All bedrooms are generously sized and comfortably take a queen bed, with the upstairs master bedroom being particularly large. The original pine beams in the peaked ceiling upstairs add character, with the window of the west-facing upstairs bedroom providing pleasant sea views towards the horizon.\r\n\r\nThe rear of the house faces just a few degrees to the east side of due north, allowing for plentiful natural light in the main living area with the rear deck and stairs a great place to relax and enjoy the birdsong. The mature liquid amber tree provides stunning coloured foliage at different times of the year, before dropping its leaves to let more light in over winter months. Close to the regional park and with tree life in abundance, the view from the kitchen includes local tui feeding on the flowering aloe vera, while out back, brightly coloured rosellas, tui and grey warblers are often seen and heard in the liquid amber and pohutukawa trees.\r\n\r\nBus stops for buses in either direction (towards the regional park, Gulf Harbour, Whangaparaoa town centre, Silverdale) are handily located within 50m of the front gate, while Gulf Harbour marina, shops and restaurants are a 3 minute drive, and the Gulf Harbour Ferry pier (50 min to CBD) is 7 minutes drive. Three separate boat ramps are located within 5 minutes drive and Whangaparaoa Golf Club is just 600m away. \r\n\r\nSince moving out, the current owners have stayed in Army Bay for the lifestyle it offers, being close to great beaches, excellent playgrounds for the kids, good fishing and nature walks, yet in touch of the CBD via ferry for work. Local schooling includes Gulf Harbour School and Wentworth College & Primary. Whangaparaoa town centre (10 min drive) and Silverdale (20 min drive) are close for shopping and groceries and with O Mahurangi Penlink due for completion in 3 years, driving time to the city is expected to shorten.\r\n\r\n1396 Whangaparaoa Road is vacant and ready for immediate possession.\r\n\r\nLIM and Title documents available on request.",
